  "final_report": {
    "critique": [
      {
        "dimension": "silhouette_scale_hierarchy",
        "evidence": "The overhead basalt roof and opposing upper platforms frame a striking central breach; quartz, the gate and signal totem form readable vertical landmarks. Some silhouettes at the two damaged central structures are visually busy at this scene scale.",
        "score_0_to_5": 4
      },
      {
        "dimension": "architectural_geologic_richness",
        "evidence": "The capture shows varied ceiling teeth, stratified rock edges, interrupted decks, piers and multiple levels of service structures, making the environment feel site-specific rather than a repeated platform strip.",
        "score_0_to_5": 5
      },
      {
        "dimension": "authentic_micro_detail",
        "evidence": "Rust, rails, cables, instrument marks and small lights create convincing authored texture. In the central collapse area, numerous fine elements compete and lose legibility at the full panorama scale.",
        "score_0_to_5": 4
      },
      {
        "dimension": "value_colour_discipline",
        "evidence": "Dark rock and void dominate while cyan, amber and quartz accents provide focal contrast. Bright accents are generally restrained, though the dense center concentrates many competing bright marks.",
        "score_0_to_5": 4
      },
      {
        "dimension": "environmental_narrative",
        "evidence": "The severed central datum, broken spans, survey instruments and isolated tiered courts communicate a damaged underground calibration site; the void is an effective narrative element.",
        "score_0_to_5": 5
      },
      {
        "dimension": "coherent_integrated_composition",
        "evidence": "The architectural and geological masses relate across both sides of the central rupture, and the upper/lower levels establish coherent depth. The center is intentionally disordered but could benefit from a slightly stronger focal hierarchy.",
        "score_0_to_5": 4
      },
      {
        "dimension": "cross_theme_distinctiveness",
        "evidence": "Basalt, quartz and survey apparatus give the setting a distinct geological-instrumental identity, differentiated from a generic industrial ruin.",
        "score_0_to_5": 4
      }
    ],
    "edits_applied": [],
    "outcome": "critique_only",
    "revision_proposals": [
      {
        "change": "At matched full-scene scale, test reducing or consolidating a few of the smallest bright rail/cable indicators immediately around the breach, keeping the paired broken register faces as the dominant focal cue.",
        "rationale": "The capture's central collapse is narratively strong but locally dense; selective subtraction may improve focal legibility without changing the larger silhouette.",
        "target": "Central Severed Datum Exchange in the flagship scene"
      },
      {
        "change": "Review whether the repeated thin orange deck-edge marks can be grouped into a few purposeful damaged or instrumented sections rather than read as a near-continuous highlight.",
        "rationale": "A more selective warm accent rhythm could further separate structural silhouette from small instrumentation.",
        "target": "Platform and deck accents across the flagship"
      }
    ],
    "summary": "Reviewed the verified Godot full-scene capture and baseline pack. The composition is already unusually developed, with a clear central rupture and layered survey-station narrative; I made no edits rather than risk disturbing the tightly authored geometry without identifying a specific safe improvement.",
    "validation_notes": "Baseline validator passed: 8 source-checked authoring pieces with bounds, variant and classification checks; native execution was not performed. No edits were made, so no post-edit validation or render comparison was run. Visual critique is based on the verified input Godot capture; no after-capture improvement is claimed.",
